# Compose interpolation for one concert-tickets component on a server; Compose 2.40.3+.
# From demo/concert-tickets, copy this file outside the checkout and edit the paths:
#   docker compose --env-file /srv/hilos/concert-tickets.env -p tickets-galera1 -f docker/cluster/database.yml config
#   docker compose --env-file /srv/hilos/concert-tickets.env -p tickets-proxy -f docker/cluster/proxy.yml config
#   docker compose --env-file /srv/hilos/concert-tickets.env -p tickets-m1 -f docker/cluster/node.yml config
#   docker compose --env-file /srv/hilos/concert-tickets.env -p tickets-entry -f docker/cluster/entry.yml config
# Replace config with up -d --build only after provisioning these inputs. Vendor and
# frontend builds remain existing prerequisites; this does not provision remote hosts.
# --env-file supplies Compose interpolation. HILOS_CLUSTER_NODE_ENV selects a separate
# runtime env file loaded after common.env. Paths in this file resolve from docker/cluster.
# Use a different Compose project per component on one Docker engine.

# The selected runtime file (for this example m1) supplies the node's own identity and
# routable addresses. Copy nodes/m1.env to this path and edit it for the real hosts:
#   APP_ENV=dev
#   DB_HOST=192.0.2.10
#   DB_PORT=3306
#   DB_DATABASE=hilos-demo-concert-tickets-cluster
#   DB_USERNAME=hilos
#   DB_PASSWORD=replace-with-the-database-password
#   CLUSTER_NODE_ID=m1
#   CLUSTER_NODE_NAME=Master 1
#   CLUSTER_NODE_ROLE=master
#   CLUSTER_NODE_CAPABILITIES=worker,ram=10,slots=64
#   CLUSTER_PEER_HOST=0.0.0.0
#   CLUSTER_PEER_PORT=8095
#   CLUSTER_PEER_ADVERTISE=192.0.2.11:18095
#   CLUSTER_SEEDS=192.0.2.12:28095,192.0.2.13:38095,192.0.2.14:48095,192.0.2.15:58095
#   CLUSTER_MASTER_SET=m1,m2,m3,m4,m5
#   HILOS_TRUSTED_PROXIES=192.0.2.30/32
#   CLUSTER_TLS_CA_FILE=/app/docker/tls/ca.pem
#   CLUSTER_TLS_CERT_FILE=/app/docker/tls/m1.pem
#   MAIL_SMTP_HOST=192.0.2.20
#   MAIL_SMTP_PORT=1025
# Seeds exclude this node's advertise endpoint. Provision matching TLS files under
# the mounted project before starting. The peers share one master set and database.
HILOS_CLUSTER_NODE_ENV=/srv/hilos/m1.env
HILOS_CLUSTER_LOG_DIR=/srv/hilos/logs/m1
# Every node and the entry must see this same, pre-provisioned shared export storage.
# The bind uses an existing shared directory; it provisions no storage service.
# The published files directory, data/files/published, is shared the same way through
# the project bind of the nodes and the entry's own bind of it.
HILOS_CLUSTER_DATA_EXPORT_DIR=/srv/hilos/shared/data_export
# The DB directory is persistent server storage; local stands default to /dev/shm.
HILOS_CLUSTER_DB_DATA_DIR=/srv/hilos/mysql
# Local CLI only: the tracked test env is mounted read-only at /app/tests/.env.
HILOS_CLUSTER_TEST_ENV_FILE=../../tests/.env

# MariaDB initialization credentials; match the selected node runtime DB values.
# The data member part mounts the journal script on every member: a fresh or an existing
# cluster gets the Change Log journal by running provision-change-log.sh ONCE with these root
# credentials on the first data member, after that member is Synced and before the nodes
# start; Galera replicates the journal to the other data members. Only the local stand's
# galera1 also mounts the init hook that runs it by itself on a fresh stand.
DB_DATABASE=hilos-demo-concert-tickets-cluster
DB_USERNAME=hilos
DB_PASSWORD=replace-with-the-database-password
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=replace-with-the-root-password

# One Galera data member, the one this file starts. Every member names the same cluster and
# the same address list: every data member, comma-separated. The member raises a new cluster
# only when none of HILOS_GALERA_DATA_PEERS (the OTHER data members, space-separated) answers
# on 4567, and joins otherwise - so start the members one at a time. The part publishes only
# SQL: the replication ports 4567, 4568 and 4444 and the agent port 9200 must be reachable
# between the servers by the operator's own means.
HILOS_GALERA_CLUSTER_NAME=hilos-concert-tickets-cluster
HILOS_GALERA_CLUSTER_ADDRESS=192.0.2.31,192.0.2.32,192.0.2.33
HILOS_GALERA_NODE_NAME=galera1
HILOS_GALERA_NODE_ADDRESS=192.0.2.31
HILOS_GALERA_DATA_PEERS="192.0.2.32 192.0.2.33"

# The proxy: the three data members, each a complete host:port of its SQL.
HILOS_CLUSTER_GALERA_BACKEND_1=192.0.2.31:3306
HILOS_CLUSTER_GALERA_BACKEND_2=192.0.2.32:3306
HILOS_CLUSTER_GALERA_BACKEND_3=192.0.2.33:3306

# Bind published database, peer, WebSocket, HTTP and entry ports on the server interface.
# The database port is published by a data member and by the proxy, each on its own server.
HILOS_CLUSTER_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0
HILOS_CLUSTER_DB_PUBLISHED_PORT=3306
HILOS_CLUSTER_PEER_PUBLISHED_PORT=18095
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_PUBLISHED_PORT=18092
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_PUBLISHED_PORT=18090
HILOS_CLUSTER_ENTRY_HTTP_PUBLISHED_PORT=80
HILOS_CLUSTER_ENTRY_HTTPS_PUBLISHED_PORT=443
# Worker IPC and command ports are deliberately not published.

# Full nginx upstream endpoints; values are complete host:port pairs.
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_M1=192.0.2.11:18092
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_M2=192.0.2.12:28092
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_M3=192.0.2.13:38092
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_M4=192.0.2.14:48092
HILOS_CLUSTER_WS_M5=192.0.2.15:58092
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_M1=192.0.2.11:18090
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_M2=192.0.2.12:28090
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_M3=192.0.2.13:38090
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_M4=192.0.2.14:48090
HILOS_CLUSTER_HTTP_M5=192.0.2.15:58090

# Existing stand namespace/weight values pass through the root include and env files.
# HILOS_STAND_SUFFIX=-s3
# HILOS_STAND_CPU_SHARES=64
# HILOS_STAND_NET_CONCERT_TICKETS_CLUSTER=60
# Do not use deployment interpolation with the local aggregate: node identities and
# local published ports are fixed there. Local exports and published files keep the
# stand's named volumes.
